  "goodToKnow": "Die Sozialwissenschaft, usually plural Sozialwissenschaften, is social science: sociology, political science, economics and related fields. German thinkers shaped it: Max Weber, Georg Simmel, Karl Marx and the Frankfurt School (Adorno, Horkheimer, Habermas). In German, Wissenschaft covers all scholarly disciplines, including humanities (Geisteswissenschaften). Der Sozialwissenschaftler is a social scientist. Plural: die Sozialwissenschaften."
